#israel #gaza #ceasefire 
The humanitarian situation in Gaza is dire, with over 27,000 people killed and 66,000 wounded in Israeli attacks since October 7. Despite efforts to deliver aid, a convoy of trucks carrying food into Gaza was hit by Israeli fire, damaging essential supplies. Medical facilities are overwhelmed, with Al-Shifa Hospital experiencing a rapid deterioration, leading to a surge in patients at Ahli Arab Hospital. Thousands of people urgently need evacuation for medical care, and humanitarian missions are being restricted by Israeli authorities. International aid efforts are underway, but the situation remains critical.
